      "text": "Bedford Township was founded in 1823 and later renamed Bedford when Township 6 became a village that year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bedford%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Hezekiah Dunham House, built in 1832, still stands as one of Historic Bedford’s most famous homes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://clevelandhistorical.org/items/show/885"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Transportation history surged when the Ohio and Erie Canal opened in 1827 and the Cleveland & Pittsburgh Railroad began in 1852.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bedford%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Both the Hezekiah Dunham House and the Old Town Hall are listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
